logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-e2e
dist-ssr
dist-flag-off
*.local

# Test runner output (vitest / playwright)
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# The one exception, and it is not a secret. `VITE_PROXY_BASE_URL` is a public
# API Gateway endpoint that ships INSIDE the bundle — the browser has to know it
# to play, so it is published the moment the game deploys. contract-calls §11
# says so outright: "It is not a secret; the origin check and throttling are the
# access control", and the only real secret in the system stays in the Lambda
# (physical §2 constraint 2).
#
# It is committed rather than passed as a repository variable because
# `deploy.yml`'s build step is a bare `npm run build` with no `env:` and no
# `${{ vars.* }}`, and that workflow may not change (physical §2 constraint 4).
# Vite reads this file itself on a production build, so nothing else has to.
!.env.production

# Super-pipeline runtime state must stay out of git
.claude/super/

